<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33270" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκχράω</span></b>  (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χράω</span> c), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>declare as
				an oracle, tell out</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πόλλ᾽ . . ὅτ᾽ ἐξέχρη κακά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					87
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>suffice</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἐξέχρησέ σφι ἡ ἡμέρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.70
				</span></i>
			: impers., c. inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς
				ταῦτα βασιλέϊ ἐκχρήσει περιυβρίσθαι</span>; how
				<i>will it suffice</i> him, how <i>will he be content</i> to
			. . ? <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.137
			</span></i>.</div>
